          '`src/world/buildings/citadel/build.js` `decorateCitadel(instance, ctx)` (everything via `instance.addDetail`): `curtainWall` on the south (w 22, at z 9), east (w 18, at x 11, rot 1.5708) and west (w 18, at x -11, rot -1.5708) facades (the north facade is a solid `concrete` core wall); the canopy over `main`; `signboard({ key: "gravitywrite", w: 6.0, h: 1.1, style: "board" })` lit, on the canopy fascia at (0, 4.4, 12.0), and a second `signboard({ key: "gravitywrite", w: 3.0, h: 0.8, style: "plaque" })` on the east facade at (11.1, 3.2, 6.0) (declared `signage` 2, both register their lights in group `citadel:sign`, `auto: "dusk"`); planters 6 at (-9.0, 10.0), (-6.0, 10.0), (6.0, 10.0), (9.0, 10.0), (-11.8, 6.0), (11.8, 6.0); bins 3 at (-11.7, 2.0), (11.7, 2.0), (-11.7, -3.0); wall lamps 8 (each registers a light in group `citadel:exterior`, `auto: "dusk"`) at the south wall x -3.0, 3.0, -8.0, 8.0 (y 3.0, z 9), east (11, 2.0), west (-11, 2.0), beside the service door (-11, -3.6) and north (0, -9, rot 3.1416); the rooftop `waterTank`, `antennaPair` and `glassRailParapet`; the `flagpole`. Emissive bands: `decorateCitadel` registers the three bands (the `bandMeshes` of each wall) through the same light registration the kit uses for building lights (`registerLight({ id: "citadel:band-s" | "citadel:band-e" | "citadel:band-w", x, y: 4.8, z, color: "#9fe8ff", intensity: 0, distance: 1, group: "citadel:bands", auto: "dusk", emissive: bandMeshes })`, emissive only: they glow at dusk and are dark by day). Plan 046 only verifies them.',
          'Signage: add TWO keys to `src/content/signage.js` (the existing signage module; read how plan 025 and 042 add keys): `gravitywrite` `{ en: "GRAVITYWRITE", ta: "கிராவிட்டிரைட்" }` (uppercase on the board, the brand is written GravityWrite elsewhere) and `citadel-welcome` `{ en: "WELCOME", ta: "நல்வரவு" }`. No digits in keys (plan 025 rule). The Tamil of both is a draft: it goes to the human check.',
          '`tests/unit/kit/curtainWall.test.js` first (new file, frozen): finite geometry; pane count equals rows times columns for the three walls (60, 48, 48) and for one hand case (w 4.5, 2 floors gives 3 columns, 6 panes); column rule `Math.round(w / mullionEvery)` (w 22 gives 15, w 18 gives 12); spandrel y positions are exactly the four slab lines [4.8, 9.0, 13.2, 17.4]; merged mesh count at most 6 (actually 4); the mullion material name is `metalBrushed`; the glass opacity is 0.35 and the registered `glass` still has opacity 0.25; the band material has `emissiveIntensity` greater than 0.',
